        <span style="font-size:2rem;font-weight:800">~4,400<span style="font-size:1rem;font-weight:600">&nbsp;machine-checked theorems</span></span>
        <span style="font-size:2rem;font-weight:800">0<span style="font-size:1rem;font-weight:600">&nbsp;axioms beyond Lean's standard three</span></span>
      </div>
      <p style="margin:.2rem 0 0;font-size:1.05rem"><strong>Headlines:</strong>
        the <strong>von Neumann double-commutant theorem</strong> (A″ = SOT = WOT closure — a Mathlib gap, closed) ·
        the <strong>Araki–Woods III₁ fingerprint</strong> of the capacity code tower (first machine contact with the Type III₁ wall) ·
        <strong><code>towerLimitVN</code></strong> — the tower's inductive-limit von Neumann algebra, built by GNS, now with a <strong>strongly continuous unitary modular dynamics and its self-adjoint generator, a cyclic–separating vector, the closed Tomita operator S̄, the self-adjoint modular operator Δ, the modular unitary group Δ^it = the physical dynamics (the exponential-recovery wall, crossed), the modular conjugation J with the polar decomposition S̄ = J∘Δ^½ and Tomita's theorem both halves — first Δ^it M Δ^−it = M, second (inclusion) J M J ⊆ M′ — and a genuine non-tracial KMS state (Δ ≠ 1): the tower's Tomita–Takesaki modular theory now complete, the first in any proof assistant</strong> ·
        the <strong>holographic count as a theorem</strong> (S = Σ log D = A/4G, finite branch) ·
        <strong>Einstein's equations</strong> from the capacity bound (conditional Jacobson chain, free field, end to end).
